# Default apps on macOS, applied with: duti ~/.config/duti/defaults.duti
# Format: bundle_id  UTI  role. duti's settings file does not accept
# extensions, so types with no system UTI use the dynamic UTI macOS derives
# from the extension (UTType(filenameExtension:)), named in a comment above.

# Text and code: kitty opens text files in $EDITOR (nvim)
